 "notes": "Shared p4-component-program-v2 vectors. runtime: a complete valid v2 package (program engine p4-component-program-v2, image engine p4-integer-program-v2: code <=1024, fuel <=16384 with the same 64-per-turn quantum, cells <=256, opcodes TEXT a,b / CELLGET a,b,c / CELLSET a,b,c). The package cells grid is mirrored into VM cells [0, cols*rows) (row-major), so transitions may only read it; the package texts count bounds TEXT. reject: JSON-pointer patches every validator must refuse. v1ImageReject: patches to the v1 contract runtime (component-program-v1.json) that a v2 build must still refuse, because a v1 image keeps the v1 budgets and op table. cases: events run through the shared C core; expected outputs are the projected variables after the commit, cells the VM cell values, grid the clamped p4-cells-v1 rows. Devices advertise widgetProgram p4-component-program-v2 and list both engines in widgetPrograms; v1 packages stay valid. A reject entry with scope \"package\" is refused by the whole-package validators (Python, Rust, firmware runtime parser) but is outside the component-program descriptor parser itself.",
